# Getting Started

## Purpose of the Developer Portal

The Developer Portal provides a single place for users to discover:

1. Product and platform documentation.
2. Technical guidance and standards.
3. Runbooks and operational guidance.
4. API and integration information.

## New contributor onboarding path

```mermaid
flowchart TB
	A[Identify documentation need] --> B[Choose content type]
	B --> C[Find owning repository]
	C --> D[Set up local preview]
	D --> E[Create or update content]
	E --> F[Run checks locally]
	F --> G[Open PR for review]
	G --> H[Merge and verify published output]
```

## Who can publish content

Content can be published by teams with ownership of product/platform documentation and access to the relevant source repositories.

Typical contributors:

1. Engineering teams.
2. Platform teams.
3. Developer Experience contributors.
4. Documentation maintainers.

## Prerequisites for contributors

1. Access to the relevant source repository.
2. Ability to open pull requests.
3. Local tooling for preview and validation.
4. Understanding of basic markdown and frontmatter.

## Contribution workflow overview

1. Create or update content in the source repository.
2. Open a pull request for review.
3. Pass validation checks (lint/tests/link checks where applicable).
4. Post for review in [#ask-developer-experience](https://moj.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0AJBK3P5A8) slack channel.
5. Merge approved changes.
6. Confirm ingestion/publishing workflow updates portal content.


